# Panel 186 R7, lane land186, 2026-10-02: a group's record over a C union is
# built naming exactly one member of each union, so a construction may name
# fewer fields than the record declares, and `check` holds only its labels
# (`selfhost/check/group_fields.hero`); what it leaves out is `build`'s.
#
# Every field a construction leaves out that shares no byte with one it names
# is told in ONE diagnostic, naming each. clang prints one failed assertion
# per field at the construction's line and the mapper keeps one diagnostic per
# span, so R7's prototype told `y` and, on the next build, `z`.

extern "ffi-a-construction.h"
    record PT3
        x: i32
        y: i32
        z: i32
    function pt3_z(p: PT3) -> i32

function main()
    p = PT3(x: 1)  #~ missing_fields
    print(pt3_z(p))
